// EXPECT: division by zero
// `int` division by zero used to be a raw SIGFPE and a core dump with no
// message, while the same mistake on a `word` printed one line and exited 1.
// The divisor comes from argc so no constant-folding can remove the division.
main(int argc, string[] argv) {
  int z = argc - 1;
  print(10 / z);
} return int 0;
